> solve x = 1 mod 2, x = 2 mod 3
the system
  x = 1 mod 2: x = 1
    x = 1 (mod 2)
  x = 2 mod 3: x = 2
    x = 2 (mod 3)
x = 5 (mod 6)
  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)
  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..5: 1 solution
